WEBVTT

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:05.740
I hear taiko drums somewhere.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.180
From the city.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.270
It's the Yoimiya Festival today.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:10.760
A festival?

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.500
Bikuni-sama told me about them.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.220
You've never seen a festival before, Yuzu-chan?

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.680
Like, there are huge floats, 
horses climbing up cliffs,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.370
tons of food, and people run 
toward the gods at full speed...

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.190
You've got a bunch of stuff mixed up.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.080
But yeah, something like that.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.400
That's right.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.040
And after the festival, they set it all 
on fire, and everyone dances around it.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.610
You're making it even worse.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:43.040
All right, let's take Yun-tan 
to a real festival today.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:46.010
What are we going to do about work, silly?

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.910
The guests are all going 
to the festival, anyway.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.980
I think we can go then.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:54.200
Let's split up into two 
groups and take turns.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.650
Okami and I will be here the whole time.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.280
So will Okiku.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.660
But going out during work?

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.400
Come on, why not?

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.620
It won't be any fun without you there.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:12.790
W-Well, if everyone else is going, 
I don't have any reason to say no.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:14.360
I'll stay behind.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.910
I'm not particularly interested.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:17.610
You're going, too, Satsuki.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:27.060
If you don't go, these two are going to be 
wandering around town by themselves.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.970
They can't go with Ren or Natsume because they 
have guests to attend to at different times.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:03:02.990
<b>Konohana Kitan</b>

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:08.000
<b>Episode 7: 
Night of the Summer Festival</b>

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.370
We'll be off now.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:17.550
<b>Konohanatei</b>

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.230
Well, then, let's get back to work.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:19.650
You two will be going 
when those girls get back.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.200
Are you sure you don't want to go?

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.570
I'm too old for bon dances 
and street vendors.

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:28.720
How old are you, Kiri-san?

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.140
Sure, I had my share of 
adventures back in my day.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.660
How old are you, Kiri-san?

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:38.430
I hope you girls make yourselves 
some summer memories, too.

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:39.460
How old are you—

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:40.100
Ow.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.280
<b>Fried Ayu</b>

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.330
It's so lively.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:50.060
It's not like the festivals 
I've imagined, though.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.290
I'm sure.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.980
Sakura-chan, you mustn't run!

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.930
You'll crash into peopl—

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.220
Are you all right?

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.190
Yes.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.270
Sakura-chan, wait for me!

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:09.710
You'll get lost if you go alone.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.260
<b>Hairpins</b>

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.720
<b>Stuffed Squid</b>

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.940
Look at that huge stuffed squid!

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.930
I don't think the three 
of us could finish it.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.140
Should we bring some back 
home for the others?

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:35.200
The other two got lost, 
and it's all my fault!

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.160
Yo, lost kid.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.700
My, what cute children.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.140
We won't get lost now.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.440
<i>I'm not a kid.</i>

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.390
<i>I don't want to hold hands.</i>

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.050
Satsuki-chan.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:49.670
Satsuki-chan.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.430
Yeah?

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:56.380
I'd like to buy you something in return for 
the shiratama zenzai you got me before.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.860
Then... get that.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.050
You have four ears now, Satsuki-chan.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:10.440
<i>Now I don't have to worry about 
bumping into people I know.</i>

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.630
It's like glass art.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.930
I could never bring myself to eat it.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:43.370
Oh, yeah. We have to buy gifts 
for Kiri-san and Okami-san.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.090
What do you think they would appreciate?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.650
That's fantastic! {tl- not sure this needs to be subbed}

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:53.410
I'm sure they would <i>really</i> appreciate that,

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.800
but how about something with 
a bit more sentimentality?

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.230
Is that the bon dance?

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:10.840
Yeah.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.910
It's to invite the spirits 
and give them comfort.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:17.550
Today is when souls come 
back from the afterlife.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:21.710
The souls arrive on fast horses,

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:26.550
and ride home slowly on oxen 
so they can take in the scenery.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.810
Wow!

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:29.020
That sounds fun.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.760
Satsuki-chan, why don't we dance?

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:35.800
I'll pass.

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:37.640
You two go ahead.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:42.050
Okay, Sakura-chan, let's go.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:07.190
<i>All these total strangers gather around 
a tower and go around and around.</i>

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:17.420
<i>I feel like there might really be people 
from the afterlife here, too.</i>

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:23.050
Oh, stop it! I'm not <i>that</i> old.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.830
My apologies.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.250
Okami, what's that?

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:33.210
Damn it! I was crafted by a top-tier artisan.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.280
Why should I be doing this?

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.750
She's our apprentice.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.750
This is humiliating!

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.200
They need to treat dolls with more respect!

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.200
She's gone through some things, 
and we're taking care of her now.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:41.680
But isn't that...

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.640
Absolutely humiliating!

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.730
Yes, she's a doll.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:47.890
We were asked to give it a cleansing, 
but she ended up staying with us.

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:49.230
I see.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.680
Being here would be a 
good cleansing in itself.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:56.550
She still has some problems, 
so we can't let her go outside yet.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:59.610
Four more hot sake.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:01.070
Okay, got it.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.860
Hey, has there always been so few people?

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:05.270
Where's everyone else?

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:07.130
Oh, everyone else is...

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:11.220
Why can't I go to the festival?!

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:16.360
It's not that you can't, but Okami 
says it might still be dangerous.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.200
Dangerous how?

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.430
You haven't been here for very long yet.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.710
What?!

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:23.610
This is newcomer harassment!

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:26.730
Fine, I'll just sue you!

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:31.600
People like you tend to get taken 
to the other side. That's why.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.560
The other side?

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.620
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:39.480
<i>The tower's gotten to be so far away.</i>

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:42.230
<i>I'm sure we've been by here already.</i>

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:45.020
<i>Were there so many people here before?</i>

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.450
Where are you all headed?

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:49.380
Where else?

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.660
We're going home.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:53.470
On the backs of oxen, taken by the smoke.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.800
We have to hurry, or the gate will close.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.510
You'd better hurry, too, lady.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.380
<i>I'm not going.</i>

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:09.080
<i>That's not where I belong.</i>

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.590
<i>My home is with...</i>

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:18.520
Yuzu?

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.410
It <i>is</i> you.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:25.050
You shouldn't be 
following us out here again.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.160
Home for you is that way.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.620
Go straight. Don't get lost.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:35.640
Thank you for the kind advice.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.630
I'm just returning the favor.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:41.840
Anyway, I have to get going, too.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:49.180
See you again, Yuzu.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.800
Damn it, where did she wander off to?

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:12.390
You're late!

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:14.190
It's time to go home.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.100
Hey, Yuzu.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:17.600
Huh?

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.890
Sorry! I was dancing, and I got lost.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:24.710
How do you get lost going in circles?

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:26.500
I'm sorry.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:41.120
Someone very kind helped me, though.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:43.280
What?

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:48.550
I wonder if she'll be back next year.

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:57.920
<b>Konohanatei</b>

00:10:58.210 --> 00:11:01.340
You go ahead and help Kiri 
at the banquet tables for me.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:02.800
I'll head to the kitchen.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.000
Understood.

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:05.840
Huh?

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:10.560
You didn't go to the festival, Okiku-chan?

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.770
I hate huge crowds.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:17.430
I prefer to enjoy the atmosphere quietly.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:29.330
<b>Balloons</b>

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:28.860
<i>It was like this before, too.</i>

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:32.120
<i>A new yukata, new sandals...</i>

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:36.830
<i>I kept checking in the mirror to make 
sure I was prettier than everyone else.</i>

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.950
<i>Didn't I learn my lesson then?</i>

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:43.040
Whoa! This dude's amazing!

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:45.190
He's too quick for the eye!

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:47.630
<i>She doesn't notice that kind of thing.</i>

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:49.860
<i>I don't get it.</i>

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:52.350
<i>Nothing's changed since we were little.</i>

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.510
What should I have?

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:56.030
<i>We've both grown up.</i>

00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:59.070
<i>Aren't there more mature ways to have fun?</i>

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.530
<b>Okonomiyaki</b>

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.520
Come on...

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.700
Hey, Ren, how about some candy appl—

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:08.220
I-I think it's too soon for that.

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:09.820
You're right.

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:11.560
Candy apples are dessert.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:14.040
All right, let's start with takoyaki!

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:19.910
<i>It's just like before.</i>

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:24.100
<i>I got all dressed up, 
and she didn't even notice.</i>

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:28.080
<b>Cotton Candy</b>

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.800
<i>She left me behind and ran around.</i>

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:31.840
<i>I was so sad, I went home without 
even watching the fireworks.</i>

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:37.190
<i>Because of that, I don't have any 
good memories of festivals.</i>

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:39.840
Look at that huge stuffed squid!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.430
How many minutes do you think 
it'll take me to eat it by myself?

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:44.390
<i>I've grown up, too.</i>

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:46.380
<i>I don't get angry over that kind of thing.</i>

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:48.420
Ren, let's go over there!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.460
They have a shooting range!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.370
This way!

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:56.400
<i>Oh, no.</i>

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.140
<i>I hope my hair hasn't fallen out of place.</i>

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:00.090
<i>It took me a lot of time to braid it.</i>

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.690
<i>My new sandals are chafing me...</i>

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.210
<i>But...</i>

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:10.800
I hope you girls make yourselves 
some summer memories, too.

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:12.780
<i>Patience.</i>

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:15.470
Ren...

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.290
Yes?

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:18.700
Aren't you having fun?

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:20.480
I-I am.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.220
Really?

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:23.800
You've been so quiet.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.940
I thought you weren't having fun.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:28.900
<i>Be nicer to me if you noticed!</i>

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:30.540
<i>I'm trying to put up with you!</i>

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:34.440
<i>Why don't you compliment me 
after all the effort I put in?</i>

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:36.780
<i>Go drown in stuffed squid 
and return to the sea!</i>

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:40.250
<i>Not that I'd say that.</i>

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:41.520
Nah, I'm just a little tired from walking.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:42.530
Really?

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.640
Don't be a wimp. You'll make it sound bad.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.390
Swing bigger!

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:51.410
Men!

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.410
A-And they're naked!

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:57.120
Stay here for a sec.

00:13:57.660 --> 00:13:58.910
Nacchan...

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.900
Guys, can I join?

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.110
Look, we've got a twig here.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.570
Can you play the taiko?

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:08.700
I can.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.020
I've seen it before.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:11.380
Get up here, then.

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:12.400
Sweet!

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:26.850
<i>Nacchan's eyes are like 
gems when she's serious.</i>

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.980
That guy's so awesome!

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:52.370
I know. He's so skinny, too.

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.360
So gorgeous!

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.950
<i>Of course she's awesome.</i>

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:58.660
<i>There's nothing Nacchan can't 
do when she gets serious.</i>

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:10.800
Thanks, Pops.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.830
That was pretty impressive.

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:15.940
That was amazing.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:17.260
What's your name?

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.890
I wish I had a boyfriend like him.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:24.960
I know.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.970
<i>My hair's fallen out of place.</i>

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:32.620
<i>My feet hurt.</i>

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:35.970
<i>I wore these new sandals for nothing.</i>

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:43.390
<i>I'm dressing up and wearing new sandals 
for my own sake. I know that.</i>

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:46.690
<i>I don't have any confidence 
when I don't look sharp.</i>

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:50.660
<i>Because there's a real gem 
next to me all the time.</i>

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:54.240
I haven't grown.

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:56.680
It's the same as before.

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:02.220
So they <i>are</i> chafing you.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:05.440
You seemed down, 
so I thought they might be.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:07.840
Why didn't you tell me?

00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:07.840
Oh, he has a girlfriend.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.000
That's no surprise.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.730
Do you want me to carry you, 
or do you want a piggyback ride?

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:11.520
I wouldn't mind him carrying me like that.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:10.410
What?

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:11.910
Well, you can't walk, can you?

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:13.620
I-I can walk.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:14.880
I don't need either.

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:22.520
Oh, yeah.

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:24.400
I forgot about the fireworks.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:27.850
We won't find a good spot in time, though.

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.570
Oh, all right.

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.330
Well, you aren't tall enough to see, are you?

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:41.470
That's how it was last time.

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:48.180
You went home because your feet were 
scraped up and hurting, remember?

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:54.860
You're wearing new sandals again, 
so I was worried.

00:16:57.830 --> 00:16:59.930
We can take a break if it hurts.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:01.170
Just tell me.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:13.450
Okay.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:24.840
Tamaya!

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.440
Kagiya!

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:32.600
It's so pretty.

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:36.540
Yeah.

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:49.540
So these are called fireworks.

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:53.730
I wonder if I'll get to go next year.

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:55.840
I hope I do.

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:35.110
I'm okay now.

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:36.190
Let me down.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:38.010
Doesn't it still hurt?

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:39.390
I'm fine.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:40.890
I want to walk barefoot.

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:49.080
The ground's still warm.

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:53.520
It's still holding the heat from 
the daytime, even this late.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:01.920
It'll be sunny tomorrow.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:05.070
Okay, let's go.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:10.750
Hey, Ren!

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:16.470
What's wrong? You just vanished.

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:17.840
Nothing's wrong.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.340
My feet hurt, so I'm going home.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.090
I'm going, too, then.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.810
You haven't seen the fireworks yet.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.320
It's fine.

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:31.840
Let's go together again.

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:35.710
Hey, the ground's not cold.

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:37.530
It was warm during the day.

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:39.320
Oh, that makes sense!

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:41.720
Why are you taking your sandals off, too?

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:44.520
It feels so good on my feet.

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:46.980
<i>I don't want to go home.</i>

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:48.800
<i>I'll be lonely.</i>

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.700
<i>I won't get to be with her once I'm home.</i>

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:54.020
Do your feet hurt?

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:55.450
No.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.030
<i>I wish we didn't have to say goodbye.</i>

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:05.320
<i>I wish we could go home to the same place.</i>

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:09.650
Let's go.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:12.530
Yeah.

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:13.570
Let's go.

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.860
To our home.

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:23.700
That hits the spot!

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:27.650
Shochu is great, but nothing beats 
cold sake during the summer.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:29.780
What's that, Sakura?

00:20:29.780 --> 00:20:30.720
A gift?

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:37.240
What is it? Let me see.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:48.480
What is this?

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:49.720
It smells sweet.

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:54.200
A squid?

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.610
It's not?

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:03.730
Did you have fun at your first festival?

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:15.260
I'm glad that you gave me your first,
more than anything.

00:21:17.220 --> 00:21:18.230
Let's eat.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:20.040
You've never had one before, have you?

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:30.690
You'll get cavities if you 
eat before bed, though.

00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:32.200
Be sure to brush your teeth.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.910
I've seen this face somewhere...

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:45.030
No, I guess not.

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:55.260
I hope we meet again.

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:58.220
Okay, then...

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:02.660
Goodnight.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Next Episode: 
Transient Guests</b>
